From dfea195cfc04237048a6031a35f860f49ccb2301 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: miromraz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:25:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: vfe-17x: stamp PIX and RDI buffers at
 their SOF

The Titan 170 PIX and RDI buffers carried the host time of the
composite or write-master done, 4-7 ms (2000x1128) or 33 ms
(4624x3468) after the frame started, while userspace wants the
exposure timing of the frame.

Stamp each buffer with the host time of its frame's start of frame
instead, still CLOCK_MONOTONIC. PIX already keeps it in the frame
token (CAMIF SOF, the frame identity the completions are validated
against). For RDI, record the RDI SOF IRQ (STATUS_0 bit 27 + n, as the
downstream rdi sof_irq_mask; the dispatch already tested that bit) per
line, after the write-master dones of the same snapshot: a frame's done
can share a snapshot with the next SOF (0.03-0.16 ms apart at full
resolution) but not with its own. The done time remains the fallback if
no SOF was seen since the output was enabled.

SOF follows the CSI-2 frame start packet, which the sensor sends as it
reads out the first row, so the time is the end of that row's
exposure; the queues keep the default TSTAMP_SRC_EOF flag, as V4L2 has
no start-of-readout source and SOE would be early by the exposure.

KUnit expectations follow the SOF timestamps; 115 CAMSS tests pass.
